{"qid": 306, "answered": null, "resp": "No answer options were provided, so I'll describe the accurate statement: neurons communicate by transmitting electrical signals (action potentials) along their axons and then releasing chemical neurotransmitters across synapses to the next cell.\n\nFINAL: Neurons communicate by sending electrical impulses (action potentials) along the axon, which trigger the release of chemical neurotransmitters at synapses that bind to receptors on the neighboring neuron.", "final": "Neurons communicate by sending electrical impulses (action potentials) along the axon, which trigger the release of chemical neurotransmitters at synapses that bind to receptors on the neighboring neuron."}
